      "title": "Error Boundaries: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Error Boundaries: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Boundary Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Error boundary== = component that catches **render** errors below it",
                "Shows a ==fallback UI== instead of unmounting the app",
                "Catches: render, lifecycle methods, constructors of descendants",
                "Error goes up to the ==nearest== boundary only"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Child throws",
                    "sub": "in render",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Nearest boundary",
                    "sub": "catches it",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fallback UI",
                    "sub": "app stays up",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Caught vs Missed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Caught",
                "Not caught"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Render",
                  "Event handlers"
                ],
                [
                  "Lifecycle methods",
                  "Async: `setTimeout`, promises, fetch callbacks"
                ],
                [
                  "Constructors",
                  "SSR errors"
                ],
                [
                  "",
                  "The boundary's own errors"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Routing Missed Errors",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Event handlers: ==try/catch==",
                "Async: catch, then rethrow via `setState` or call `showBoundary`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "try { save() } catch (err) {",
                "  setState(() => { throw err })",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "rethrown during render, so a boundary sees it"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No boundary",
              "text": "An uncaught render error unmounts the **whole tree**: blank screen."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Interview:** which errors skip a boundary? Event handlers, async code, SSR, the boundary itself.",
                "**Interview:** why throw inside `setState`? The rethrow happens in render, so a boundary catches it.",
                "**Interview:** with no boundary? The whole tree unmounts."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Class Boundaries and react-error-boundary",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Class Boundaries and react-error-boundary",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Class boundary",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`static getDerivedStateFromError(error)` returns state like ==`{ hasError: true }`== to render the fallback",
                "`componentDidCatch(error, info)` is for **side effects** such as logging; `info.componentStack` is the trace",
                "==No hooks equivalent==: a function component cannot be a boundary, so use a class or a library"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "class Boundary extends React.Component {",
                "  state = { hasError: false };",
                "  static getDerivedStateFromError(e) { return { hasError: true }; }",
                "  componentDidCatch(e, info) { log(e, info.componentStack); }",
                "  render() { return this.state.hasError ? <Fallback /> : this.props.children; }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "state sets the fallback, didCatch only logs"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. react-error-boundary",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "<ErrorBoundary FallbackComponent={Fallback}",
                "  onError={log} onReset={fn} resetKeys={[id]}>",
                "  <Profile id={id} />",
                "</ErrorBoundary>",
                "",
                "const { showBoundary } = useErrorBoundary();",
                "fetch(url).catch(showBoundary);"
              ],
              "note": "Fallback gets { error, resetErrorBoundary }"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Piece",
                "Does"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`resetErrorBoundary`",
                  "Retry: clears the error, calls `onReset`"
                ],
                [
                  "`resetKeys={[id]}`",
                  "{green:Auto-resets} when a listed value changes"
                ],
                [
                  "`showBoundary(err)`",
                  "Pushes **event handler** or **async** errors to the nearest boundary"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Class API: ==getDerivedStateFromError== sets the fallback, ==componentDidCatch== logs. Library: wrap a subtree, reset with keys."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Suspense for Loading States",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Suspense for Loading States",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Suspends",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`<Suspense fallback={<Spinner />}>` shows the ==fallback== while any child below it is **suspended**",
                "Suspends via ==lazy()==, `use(promise)`, framework data fetching, cache libraries",
                "{red:useEffect fetching} does NOT trigger Suspense"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Nesting and Updates",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Nearest ancestor== Suspense wins",
                "Nest boundaries for granular fallbacks: page shell first, widgets later",
                "Wrap updates in ==startTransition== or `useDeferredValue` so shown content stays, no revert to fallback"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "<Suspense fallback={<PageSkeleton />}>",
                "  <Header />",
                "  <Suspense fallback={<ChartSkeleton />}>",
                "    <Chart />",
                "  </Suspense>",
                "</Suspense>"
              ],
              "note": "Chart suspends: only ChartSkeleton shows"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pair with an Error Boundary",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "ErrorBoundary",
                    "sub": "outside: rejected",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Suspense",
                    "sub": "inside: pending",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Component",
                    "sub": "suspends or throws",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Order",
              "text": "Suspense handles ==pending==, the error boundary handles ==rejected==. ErrorBoundary goes **outside**, Suspense **inside**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "lazy() and Code Splitting",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "lazy() and Code Splitting",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What lazy() Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`const Page = lazy(() => import('./Page'))` defers the chunk until ==first render==",
                "The module needs a ==default export==",
                "Split by ==route== first, then heavy parts: charts, editors, modals"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Named Exports",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Export",
                "lazy() form"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Default",
                  "`lazy(() => import('./X'))`"
                ],
                [
                  "Named",
                  "wrap it as `{ default: m.X }`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const X = lazy(() =>",
                "  import('./X').then(m => ({ default: m.X }))",
                ");"
              ],
              "note": "top level of the module"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Failures and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Offline / stale deploy",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "import() rejects",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Error boundary",
                    "sub": "Retry button",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "lazy() inside a component makes a ==new type== each render, so state resets",
                "Declare lazy() at ==module top level=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Always wrap in Suspense",
              "text": "No ancestor Suspense means no fallback: the screen stays ==blank== on first render until the chunk loads. Wrap lazy components so a loading state shows."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
